      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "Find the equation of the parabola whose vertex is at $(6,-1)$ and whose leading coefficient is $-1.$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the vertex form of a parabola is\n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k,\n$$\n\nwhere $(h,k)$ are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola, and $a$ is the leading coefficient.\n\nSubstituting $(h,k)=(6,-1)$ and $a=-1$ into the above and then expanding and simplifying, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-1(x-6)^{2}+(-1) \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}-12x+36)-1 \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}+12x-36-1 \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}+12x-37.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is $y=-{x}^{2}+12x-37.$",
